  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inter-European Basic Instructor Course (IEBIC)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Inter-European Basic Instructor Course (IEBIC) is designed to prepare mid-grade enlisted and junior officers (OF-2) to serve as instructors capable of tailoring delivery methods and lessons of instruction based on the needs of their student population. IEBIC consists of lessons adopted from the Theories and Principles of Adult Education (TPAE) and the Enlisted Professional Military Education Instructor Course (EPMEIC) curriculums. Curriculum delivery is focused on achieving higher levels of learning through deliberate application of instructor skill sets. The course focuses on effective teaching techniques, including classroom management, feedback/assessment, and delivery skills. Instructional methods taught in the course include lectures, guided discussions, case studies, gamification, and experiential learning. All classes are developed using established educational theory, to which the students are also exposed. The course includes practical application and focuses on developing instructors through mentorship and actionable feedback.</narrative>
  </description>
